// boxcxx — <future>.
//
// promise / future / shared_future / packaged_task / async over the SAME
// event-driven substrate as condition_variable: every shared state carries one
// atomic<uint32_t> __ready word and nothing more for the wake. The producer
// stores the value/exception, then __ready.store(1, release) + an
// __boxcxx_atomic_notify(&__ready, true); a waiter loops load-compare on __ready
// and parks via __boxcxx_atomic_wait_cycle (the version-pool park — WAITPKG
// UMONITOR/UMWAIT on the word when present, PAUSE budget then a real kernel park
// otherwise). The acquire on the waiter's load pairs with the producer's release,
// so a future that observes __ready==1 has happens-before visibility of the
// stored result. A notify that races a waiter between its load and its park is
// never lost: the load is the predicate authority, and the substrate's
// pool-version park-gate independently stops the waiter sleeping through it.
// This is event-driven, NOT polling — the timed path rides the same merged
// timeout fix the cv/semaphore timed waits ride on (a notify returns a timed park
// EARLY, it does not burn its budget; the deadline is exact, kernel b88b313).
//
// async(launch::async) launches a std::thread (NOT a raw strand_spawn): its
// trampoline already stands up this strand's per-strand thread_local image and
// its per-strand exception bookkeeping (__boxcxx_tls_strand_init /
// __boxcxx_thread_storage_enter / exit) and the terminate-on-escape contract, so
// async inherits all of it for free. The std::thread is moved INTO the shared
// state; the LAST shared-state owner joins it exactly once in ref_dec (a
// __join_owner CAS), which is the conformant ~future blocking-join of an async
// future ([futures.async]/5 + /6). Plain (non-async) futures never arm a worker,
// so their ref_dec join is a no-op.
//
// A worker that throws does NOT publish the exception from inside its catch
// block: it captures the exception_ptr in the catch, LEAVES the catch (so the
// strand's __cxa_end_catch runs while this strand is the sole refcount owner of
// the exception object), and only THEN stores it and notifies. This is the
// capture-then-publish ordering that, together with the atomic
// __cxa_end_catch refcount, makes a cross-strand exception_ptr hand-off race-free.
//
// Cooperative, non-Unix: there is no futex naming/op, no errno table, no forced
// kill. future_errc is an honest fresh enum with its own fresh category (NOT a
// generic/system alias). A thread::id stays the strand pid. The substrate park
// IS the wake — there is no polling or timeout backstop as the primary wake path.
#ifndef BOXCXX_FUTURE
#define BOXCXX_FUTURE

